---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much does Karbon cost?', 'Karbon charges per user: Team $59/user/month and Business $89/user/month on annual billing. Monthly billing is only offered to teams of 4 or more, so a 3-person team pays annually.'],
  ['What is the cheapest Karbon alternative?', 'Financial Cents has the lowest published seat price in this comparison: Solo $19/month, Team $49/user/month and Scale $69/user/month (annual). For a 3-person firm, Team costs $147/month versus $177 on Karbon Team.'],
  ['Is TaxDome cheaper than Karbon?', 'Not for a 3-person firm on list prices. TaxDome Pro is $1,000/seat/year, about $250/month for 3 seats, paid upfront, versus $177/month on Karbon Team. TaxDome Pro includes the Bookkeeping Hub with 120 client ledger connections.'],
  ['When should a firm stay on Karbon?', 'Stay when your team runs client work out of shared email and wants it turned into tasks with AI summaries, when you want time tracking, billing, payments and engagement letters from the Team plan, or when you need the client reminders and automation listed on Business.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Karbon alternatives for bookkeeping firms: practice management with published prices"
  description="Options beyond Karbon's per-user practice management: Financial Cents, TaxDome and Double, with pricing verified Oct 2026 and cost for a 3-person, 20-client firm."
>
  <h1>Karbon alternatives</h1>
  <p>Karbon is practice management built around shared client email: email triage, workflow templates, a client portal, time tracking, billing and payments, with AI email summaries on top. It charges per user: Team $59/user/month and Business $89/user/month on annual billing, and monthly billing is only offered to teams of 4 or more. Firms look elsewhere when they want a lower seat price, an annual price for a solo practice, or a tool that also reviews the client's books before close. These are the closest options in our directory, not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs Karbon</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents</a></td>
        <td>Solo and small QBO firms that want workflows and client chasing at a lower seat price, plus an optional close add-on</td>
        <td>Solo $19/mo; Team $49/user/mo; Scale $69/user/mo (annual); Month-End Close add-on $5/client/mo</td>
        <td>Lighter on shared email than Karbon; the close add-on is QBO only</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/taxdome`}>TaxDome</a></td>
        <td>Firms that do tax and bookkeeping and want a branded client portal and mobile app, billing and workflows in one system</td>
        <td>Essentials $800/seat/yr (solo only); Pro $1,000/seat/yr; Business $1,200/seat/yr; 1-year terms, billed upfront</td>
        <td>Annual upfront billing only; the Bookkeeping Hub for uncategorized transactions syncs with QuickBooks Online</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/double`}>Double</a></td>
        <td>Bookkeeping firms whose bottleneck is month-end close and client file review, not email or tasks</td>
        <td>Per connected client on Core, Plus, Scale and Enterprise tiers; prices not published, demo first</td>
        <td>A close and client review tool, not a full practice management system: no firm-wide email triage or time and billing like Karbon</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost for a 3-person firm with 20 clients (list prices, per month)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Karbon: 3 × $59 = $177 (Team, annual) or 3 × $89 = $267 (Business, annual). A 3-person team cannot pay monthly.</li>
    <li>Financial Cents: 3 × $49 = $147 (Team, annual), or $247 with the close add-on for 20 clients (20 × $5).</li>
    <li>TaxDome: 3 × $1,000 per year = $3,000 per year, about $250 per month (Pro), paid upfront. Pro includes the Bookkeeping Hub with 120 client ledger connections.</li>
    <li>Double: not published.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to stay on Karbon</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your team runs client work out of shared email and wants it turned into tasks, with comments and AI summaries.</li>
    <li>You want time tracking, budgets, billing, payments and engagement letters included from the Team plan.</li>
    <li>You need automatic client reminders and task automation, which Karbon lists on Business.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: karbonhq.com/pricing and taxdome.com/pricing checked 2026-10-18; financial-cents.com/pricing and doublehq.com/pricing checked 2026-10-17 and 2026-10-18. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/tools/karbon`}>Karbon</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/karbon-vs-financial-cents`}>Karbon vs Financial Cents</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/double-alternatives`}>Double alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/uncategorized-transactions-tools`}>Uncategorized transactions tools</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/category/practice-management`}>All practice management tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
